Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||06:14 PM||||Which version are you using? There were some issues with older version where IE would paste the wrong clipboard contents into a message (the clipboard can hold several things and IE was getting the wrong one). The latest version of PIP solves this (v1.06).<P>If you are using a version prior to v1.06, you can download the newest version <A HREF="http://pip.pennock.nl/download.html" TARGET=_blank>here</A>. Just download the patch (instead of the complete version) and unzip it in your pip directory (usually C:\Program Files\Pip).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||09-28-2001||06:17 PM||||Mine worked earlier this year and I downloaded the newest version.  I can upload a file, and paste the link, but for some reason my images always apear as an X.  What would cause that?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||07:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>Mine worked earlier this year and I downloaded the newest version.  I can upload a file, and paste the link, but for some reason my images always apear as an X.  What would cause that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Can you post an example in this thread? It could be that your paint software is creating an image that the browser doesn't understand. Or it could be a firewall is blocking the upload. Could be a number of things.||||reg||1
